##
## FlyWeb: upstream blink_unittests whose expectations predate an intended
## change (Brave privacy feature, V8 13.1, or a port from Chrome 129-131).
## Triage: FM.39 item 3 (MOTOR-18, 26-10-2026). None is a browser bug.
##

# kBraveRoundTimeStamps rounds to 1 ms; the uniformity test still assumes
# Chromium's 5/100 µs resolution.
-TimeClamperTest.ClampingIsUniform

# Brave's video.requestVideoFrameCallback timestamps are coarsened to 1 ms.
-VideoFrameCallbackRequesterImplTest.VerifyParameters_WindowRaf

# kPrefetchPrivacyChanges (Brave) sends prefetches with no referrer.
-LinkLoaderTest.Prefetch

# V8 13.1 removed import assertions (`assert {}`); upstream rewrote the test
# for import attributes.
-ModuleRecordTest.moduleRequestsWithImportAssertions

# MeterAppearanceNoneFallbackStyle (ported) no longer creates the fallback
# element; upstream deleted this test.
-MeterShadowElementTest.LayoutObjectIsNotNeeded

# Brave's screenX/Y farbling returns integers (113 instead of 113.8).
-PointerEventManagerTest.PointerEventMovements

# Matches Chrome 131 behaviour: an empty main-frame load creates no script
# context; upstream added a <script> to the test.
-RendererResourceCoordinatorImplTest.IframeNotifications
